not modify any files):\n- Read the committed files (package.json, test/package.test.cjs) and run read-only git commands (`git log --oneline -5`, `git status --short`, `git ls-files`) to confirm the committed state.\n- Validate the work-package breakdown and produce a concise plan for the REMAINING work only: (a) run unit tests (`node --test test/package.test.cjs`) and confirm every AC is covered by a test, (b) confirm git commands exit 0 and the scaffold files are tracked/committed, (c) re-create the deleted marker `.story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed` and commit it with a targeted add (never `git add .`).\n- Optionally you may run the read-only test command `node --test test/package.test.cjs` to confirm green.\n\nReturn (concise markdown):\n1. Work package table: | id | action | status (done/pending) | verification |\n2. Remaining implementation steps (exact commands to run, in order).\n3. Gaps or risks found (e.g. AC not covered by a test, uncommitted files), or state explicitly that none were found.\n4. Success criteria checklist."}}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":83585,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e185180-d3b4-4221-b75d-dd2530f25a87","uuid":"7240f068-c545-4bb7-8169-05916790925b","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:00:28.670Z"}
